<BaseLayout title="FAQ">
  <div>
    <a href="/docs" class="back-link">← Back to documentation</a>
    <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>

    <h2>What is desktop-2fa?</h2>
    <p>An offline TOTP authenticator with a Python CLI and an early Textual terminal UI prototype. TOTP secrets are stored in a local encrypted vault.</p>

    <h2>Does it sync to the cloud?</h2>
    <p>No. Vaults stay local. Backups and transfers are user-managed.</p>

    <h2>Where is the vault stored?</h2>
    <p>The default is <code>~/.desktop-2fa/vault</code>. Use <code>--vault PATH</code> or <code>DESKTOP_2FA_VAULT</code> to choose another path.</p>

    <h2>What interfaces are available?</h2>
    <p>The CLI is the primary interface. <code>d2fa ui</code> is an early prototype that can list entries, generate codes, and copy codes; it cannot manage entries or create a missing vault.</p>

    <h2>Can I recover my password?</h2>
    <p>No. There is no reset or recovery key. Store the password securely and create a separate encrypted backup.</p>

    <h2>How do I back up or move the vault?</h2>
    <p>Run <code>d2fa backup</code> for an encrypted backup, or use <code>d2fa export</code> and <code>d2fa import</code> to move a vault. Backups are not automatic.</p>

    <h2>Can I add an otpauth URL or scan a QR code?</h2>
    <p>The CLI accepts <code>otpauth://</code> URLs with <code>d2fa add</code>. QR scanning is not listed as a current feature.</p>

    <h2>What is D2FA Watch?</h2>
    <p>A separate Wear OS app in development. The current MVP can create a vault, add accounts manually and generate TOTP codes on the watch. Managing accounts on a computer and securely transferring selected ones without cloud sync is planned; the transfer workflow is still being designed. Desktop-2FA remains free and open source. Watch is planned as a separate paid app. See <a href="/#watch">the Watch development update</a>.</p>

    <h2>What Python version do I need?</h2>
    <p>Python 3.11 or newer.</p>

    <h2>Where can I find command help or report a problem?</h2>
    <p>Run <code>d2fa --help</code> or <code>d2fa COMMAND --help</code>. Report issues in the{' '}<a href="https://github.com/wrogistefan/desktop-2fa/issues">GitHub issue tracker</a>.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
